{
 "_method": "Provenance + FULL visual pass, 2026-08-18. Every one of the 122 files was seen: 121 in four 8x4 montages at 150px composited over grey, and untitled folder/xoxo.jpeg on its own at 220px because ImageMagick's alpha-remove step fails on that JPEG; none of them is pixel art, and none is ambiguous -- they are flat-fill and gradient vector icons, rendered metallic game badges, and three JPEG stickers. Six frontier files were additionally inspected on their own at 200px, and Arrows/previous.png at 12x NEAREST because it is the lowest-colour negative in the whole corpus once alpha-only sources are gated out. No measure from the script was consulted while labelling (references/lessons.md SS23).",
 "_why_this_file_exists": "The population used to carry default_label='antialiased' with no roster, so a file dropped into any of the six folders silently joined the corpus that 148 of the negatives -- and therefore the whole specificity figure -- are counted from. A roster makes the membership a recorded claim instead of a directory listing.",
 "_correction": "The v6 handoff said this population's 3 false positives were 'systematically overstated' because some files are this tool's own outputs 'whose hard-edged verdict is CORRECT'. That is wrong, and stratifying by provenance was the wrong fix. All three are antialiased art that had already been cut out (love_transparent.gif is this tool's output from antialiased love.gif) -- the ARTWORK is still antialiased, --pixel-art on it is still destructive, and the verdict was still false. What produced them is a measure reading a plane that is blank by construction; see references/lessons.md SS29. The 3 were real, and the fix is in the script, not in the labels.",
